<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Cost Control & Job Costing</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Protect your profit margins with scientific financial control that identifies cost variances early and 
            provides clarity on project end-positions.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Granular Job Costing and Codes</h2>
        <p>
            Move beyond simple ledger accounting to granular job costing that mirrors your construction reality. 
            Establish project budgets mapped to detailed cost codes that reflect work sections, estimating 
            structures, and resource groupings. Every expense entry—from automated payroll allocation to 
            subcontractor certificates—is coded to these divisions, providing a surgical view of where 
            project capital is being deployed.
        </p>
        <p>
            Real-time integration with site resource logs ensures that labor and plant hire costs are 
            tracked daily, identifying productivity issues before they compound into major budget 
            variances.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Committed Cost and BCA Analysis</h2>
        <p>
            Understand your true financial exposure through automated committed cost tracking. As soon as a 
            purchase order is authorized or a subcontract award is made, the system recognizes the commitment 
            against the budget. This early-warning visibility identified potential budget overspends weeks 
            before an invoice even reaches the accounting office.
        </p>
        <p>
            The system provides structured Budget vs. Committed vs. Actual (BCA) analysis, enabling project 
            executives to distinguish between funds already spent, funds contractually promised, and 
            budget remaining for the duration of the project.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">CTC and Forecast Intelligence</h2>
        <p>
            Protect your final margins with integrated Cost-to-Complete (CTC) and Cost-at-Completion (CAC) 
            forecasting. By synthesizing actual expenditure with known commitments and field-work-remaining 
            data, the system provides a scientific projection of the project's financial end-position. 
            Monthly cost review (PCR) workflows within the system allow for the documentation of 
            risk provisions and forecast assumptions.
        </p>
        <p>
            High-level executive dashboards summarize CTC data across the entire project portfolio, 
            providing shareholders and boards with the visibility needed to manage group-level 
            working capital and commercial risk.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

